       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4000 mg per dose four times daily is 16,000 mg/day. That is five times the maximum daily dose of oral ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use). A single 4000 mg dose is also far above the usual 400\u2013800 mg. Doses like this risk serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and CNS and metabolic toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a decimal or unit slip, for example 400 mg four times daily (1,600 mg/day) was intended. Can you confirm the dose you want? Some typical options:\n\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nIf you really do want 4000 mg per dose, tell me and give me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably want to verify it."
